{"book":"PSA","chapter":133,"source":"hbo","verses":[1,2,3],"records":[{"id":"PSA.133.1.s1","verses":[1],"source":"שִׁ֥יר הַֽמַּעֲל֗וֹת לְדָ֫וִ֥דהִנֵּ֣ה מַה־טּ֭וֹב וּמַה־נָּעִ֑ים שֶׁ֖בֶת אַחִ֣ים גַּם־יָֽחַד׃","gloss":"The song of the ascents, of David. Look, how good and how pleasant [is the] dwelling of brothers also together.","pieces":[[1,"A song of ascents. Of David. See how good it is, how lovely, when {{gender:brothers and sisters|brothers}} live together in harmony!",null]],"L":{"1":"A song of ascents. Of David. Look, how good and how pleasant [is the] dwelling of {{gender:brothers and sisters|brothers}} — yes, together!"},"R":{"1":"A song for the journey up to Jerusalem. By David. It is so good and so pleasant when {{gender:brothers and sisters|brothers}} live together in peace!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"punctuation","tokens":["o191330010011","o191330010021","o191330010022","o191330010031","o191330010032"],"choice":"The title shares verse 1","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 120:1, the short title and the first line are counted together as verse 1, so the verse numbers are the same as in Bibles that print the title without a number.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o191330010011","o191330010022"],"choice":"a song of ascents: probably a pilgrim song","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 120:1: one of the fifteen songs probably sung by pilgrims going up to Jerusalem.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o191330010031","o191330010032"],"choice":"of David: linked with David","alternatives":["by David","for David","in David's style"],"reason":"Four of the Songs of Ascents (122, 124, 131, 133) add \"of David\", and one (127) \"of Solomon\". As elsewhere in the Psalms, \"of\" may mean the psalm is by him, belongs to a collection named for him, or is written for or about him. Some ancient copies of these titles lack the name.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m4","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191330010101"],"choice":"brothers: family, fellow members of the people","alternatives":["blood brothers sharing the family land"],"reason":"The word ('achim) is used of brothers in one family, who might live together on the family land (Deuteronomy 25:5), and of all Israelites as one family. For pilgrims gathered at a festival, the whole people is in view.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m5","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o191330010111","o191330010121"],"choice":"also together: truly as one","alternatives":[],"reason":"\"Also together\" (gam yachad) stresses the unity: not only living near one another but living as one.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191330010011","o191330010022"],"choice":"A song for the journey up to Jerusalem","alternatives":["A song of ascents"],"reason":"As in 120:1.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["L","B","R"],"category":"setting_alternative","tokens":["o191330010101"],"choice":"brothers and sisters","alternatives":["brothers"],"reason":"The word includes the whole family and people (m4); the gender setting gives the traditional \"brothers\".","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":"How good it is to live as one","status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.133.2.s1","verses":[2],"source":"כַּשֶּׁ֤מֶן הַטּ֨וֹב׀עַל־הָרֹ֗אשׁ יֹרֵ֗ד עַֽל־הַזָּקָ֥ן זְקַֽן־אַהֲרֹ֑ן שֶׁ֝יֹּרֵ֗ד עַל־פִּ֥י מִדּוֹתָֽיו׃","gloss":"Like the good oil on the head, running down on the beard, [the] beard of Aaron, which runs down on [the] opening of his robes,","pieces":[[2,"It is like the fine anointing oil on the head that flows down the beard, down Aaron's beard, and down over the collar of his robes,",null]],"L":{"2":"[It is] like the good oil on the head, running down on the beard, the beard of Aaron, which runs down on the collar of his robes,"},"R":{"2":"It is like the special oil poured on Aaron's head when he was made priest. The oil ran down his beard and onto the collar of his robes."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o191330020012","o191330020091"],"choice":"the oil on Aaron's head: the anointing of the high priest","alternatives":[],"reason":"Aaron, the first high priest, was anointed with a holy, fragrant oil poured on his head (Exodus 29:7; 30:22-33; Leviticus 8:12). The oil set him apart for God's service; its overflowing richness is the point of the picture.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191330020121"],"choice":"the opening of his robes: the collar","alternatives":["the hem"],"reason":"The word is \"mouth\" (peh): the opening of a garment for the head (Exodus 28:32). Some take it as the edge or hem.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191330020051","o191330020102"],"choice":"running down: flowing from above","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb (yarad) is used three times (verses 2-3): the oil runs down, and the dew comes down. Blessing comes down from above.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["B","R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o191330020012"],"choice":"anointing (B); poured ... when he was made priest (R)","alternatives":["the good oil"],"reason":"Balanced and Readable name the oil of the anointing (m1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.133.3.s1","verses":[3],"source":"כְּטַל־חֶרְמ֗וֹן שֶׁיֹּרֵד֮ עַל־הַרְרֵ֪י צִ֫יּ֥וֹן כִּ֤י שָׁ֨ם׀צִוָּ֣ה יְ֭הוָה אֶת־הַבְּרָכָ֑ה חַ֝יִּ֗ים עַד־הָעוֹלָֽם׃","gloss":"like [the] dew of Hermon, which runs down on [the] mountains of Zion; for there YHWH has commanded the blessing, life until forever.","pieces":[[3,"like the dew of Hermon coming down on the hills of Zion. For it is there that {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} has decreed the blessing, life without end.",null]],"L":{"3":"like the dew of Hermon, which runs down on the mountains of Zion; for there {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} has commanded the blessing: life forever."},"R":{"3":"It is like the heavy dew of Mount Hermon falling on the hills of Zion. That is where {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} has promised to bless {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} people with life that never ends."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o191330030012","o191330030021"],"choice":"the dew of Hermon: heavy, life-giving dew","alternatives":[],"reason":"Hermon is the highest mountain in the north of the land, known for snow and heavy dew. In the dry summer, dew keeps plants alive (Hosea 14:6). Hermon's dew falling on Zion, far to the south, is a picture of rich blessing coming down from above.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o191330030081"],"choice":"there: Zion","alternatives":["where brothers live together"],"reason":"\"There\" most naturally means Zion, the place just named, where the LORD's people gather; it may also point back to the unity of verse 1.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o191330030091","o191330030122"],"choice":"commanded the blessing: ordered it to come","alternatives":[],"reason":"God commands blessing as a king gives orders, and it comes (Leviticus 25:21; Deuteronomy 28:8).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o191330030122"],"choice":"to bless his people","alternatives":[],"reason":"Readable says who receives the blessing.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"}],"words":{"1":[{"id":"o191330010011","text":"שִׁ֥יר","after":" ","lemma":"שִׁיר","morph":"Ncbsc","gloss":"the.song","strong":"7892","transliteration":"šiyr","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine or feminine singular construct (of ...)"},{"id":"o191330010021","text":"הַֽ","after":"","lemma":"הַ","morph":"Td","gloss":"of","strong":"1886a","transliteration":"ha","lang":"H","parse":"Particle · definite article"},{"id":"o191330010022","text":"מַּעֲל֗וֹת","after":" ","lemma":"מַעֲלָה","morph":"Ncfpa","gloss":"the.ascents","strong":"4609","transliteration":"mmaʿălôṯ","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · feminine plural absolute"},{"id":"o191330010031","text":"לְ","after":"","lemma":"לְ","morph":"R","gloss":"of","strong":"3807a","transliteration":"lə","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o191330010032","text":"דָ֫וִ֥ד","after":"","lemma":"דָּוִד","morph":"Np","gloss":"David","strong":"1732","transliteration":"ḏāwiḏ","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · proper name"},{"id":"o191330010041","text":"הִנֵּ֣ה","after":" ","lemma":"הִנֵּה","morph":"Tm","gloss":"there!","strong":"2009","transliteration":"hinnēh","lang":"H","parse":"Particle · demonstrative"},{"id":"o191330010051","text":"מַה","after":"־","lemma":"מָה","morph":"Ti","gloss":"how!","strong":"4100","transliteration":"mah-","lang":"H","parse":"Particle · interrogative"},{"id":"o191330010061","text":"טּ֭וֹב","after":" ","lemma":"טוֹב","morph":"Aamsa","gloss":"good","strong":"2896","transliteration":"ṭṭôḇ","lang":"H","parse":"Adjective · masculine singular absolute"},{"id":"o191330010071","text":"וּ","after":"","lemma":"וְ","morph":"C","gloss":"and","strong":"2050b","transliteration":"û","lang":"H","parse":"Conjunction"},{"id":"o191330010072","text":"מַה","after":"־","lemma":"מָה","morph":"Ti","gloss":"how!","strong":"4100","transliteration":"mah-","lang":"H","parse":"Particle · interrogative"},{"id":"o191330010081","text":"נָּעִ֑ים","after":" ","lemma":"נָעִים","m